      "id": "concept-newton-leibniz-calculus-priority",
      "kind": "concept",
      "promptEs": "Newton · Leibniz · invención del cálculo",
      "questionEn": "What historical rivalry do the two matching invention claims refer to?",
      "answerEn": "Newton and Leibniz developed calculus in different forms. Newton worked earlier, while Leibniz published first and introduced notation that became widely used.",
      "noteEn": "Historians credit the two men with independent developments, followed by a bitter dispute over priority among them and their supporters. The years in the strip are compact labels for the period of their work, not publication dates.",
