      "id": "concept-derivado-calculus-pun",
      "kind": "concept",
      "promptEs": "derivado · derivada · juego de palabras",
      "questionEn": "What makes derivado a calculus pun?",
      "answerEn": "Derivado can call an idea derivative or unoriginal, while calculus studies derivatives, called derivadas in Spanish.",
      "noteEn": "The Spanish forms are close rather than identical: derivado uses the masculine singular adjective form with the neuter demonstrative eso, while the mathematical noun is feminine, la derivada. The sunglasses and title-text scream frame the pun as a CSI: Miami-style one-liner.",
